{"ts": 1784363686.0258331, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire 36-frame window. The trade dipped early (px oscillated -8 to -20 in the first ~9 minutes, giveback 26-62%) but never showed a clean directional breakdown -- it kept round-tripping back toward flat/positive rather than making new adverse lows, so I judged it noise rather than a wrong-direction entry. From minute 10 onward the thesis confirmed hard: px surged to a series of new highs (+21, +26, +38, +40, +47, +52) with only normal pullbacks (giveback 30-55% of the current leg) in between, ending the episode around +24. Nothing in this trade warranted a bail. Next time I'd watch for a genuine wrong-direction signature as: adverse excursion making a NEW low beyond the prior adverse low (not just chop within the same band) combined with HA/PROPP/KMDR fires stacking against for multiple consecutive frames without any with-direction fire -- that pattern never appeared here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 37}
